  "behavior": "Certified nearest-even scientific output with explicit decimal-place and exponent-case intent; exact rational ties and carries; caller refinement floor; typed UnknownZero, Exhausted and OutOfRange outcomes. Existing formatting traits and callers keep their implementation.",
  "retention_basis": "This adds a stronger explicit rounding/completion boundary, including typed outcomes for twelve scientific queries that reached the retained external cutoff. Its cost is reported as a distinct API contract, not claimed as a speed optimization. Focused, complete scalar, downstream and current-worktree compatibility checks pass.",
  "resource_tradeoff": "Exact zero, rational and extreme rational scales are faster in this probe. Pi, sqrt(2), huge-scaled pi and unresolved nonzero offsets cost more; pi rows are about 3.7 times the legacy approximate formatter cost. First calls on 1000 huge/tiny pi-scaled values retain 384000 requested Rust bytes, versus 168/32 in the legacy path. These are costs of a stronger explicit rounding/completion contract, not regressions introduced into existing callers. The exact-class precheck hypothesis must preserve every receipt and measure its own tradeoff; these timings do not establish that full structural facts cause all observed costs.",
  "rejected_variant": "The hypothesis did not produce the proposed allocation or retained-memory saving: every measured memory field is identical for all 28 rows. Twenty-one timing medians are slower, seven faster, with all ranges overlapping; this does not prove a timing regression or equivalence. A 16/32-byte executable reduction is insufficient reason to retain an extra runtime branch without a demonstrated higher-priority benefit. Sampling is closed and the complete candidate, passing validation and adverse samples remain retained.",
